hakios-metal: the processor's time in a draw (2026-11-12, session 7)

CommandBuffer::draw made its four work streams and the static key new for every draw (a dozen allocations and as
many copies as each grew) and RegShadow hashed and probed every register a draw writes. Now the streams and the key
are the command buffer's, cleared and refilled, and RegShadow is a table by register number in pages of 256 with a
generation for clear(). tools/drawbench.cpp measures it on the host against the fake GPU (an 85-draw pass into a
1080x2400 target, three programs in turn): 3.03 us a draw before, 2.59 after (-15 %); the 261 host tests pass.

